"""Render the current finite Drive validation checkpoint with separate source/field counts."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
F=Path(__file__).resolve().parent

def main():
 s=json.loads((F/'summary.json').read_text());state=json.loads((F/'state.json').read_text());tasks=[json.loads(l) for l in (F/'validation_tasks.jsonl').read_text().splitlines() if l];statuses=json.loads((F/'validation_status.json').read_text());finished=sum(r['status']=='completed' for r in statuses.values());reviews=[json.loads(l) for l in (F/'adjudication_tasks.jsonl').read_text().splitlines() if l];rs=json.loads((F/'adjudication_status.json').read_text());valid=[r for r in reviews if rs.get(r['key'],{}).get('validation')=='valid'];c=s['coverage'];done=state['status']=='complete'
 lines=['# Drive source follow-up', '',f"**{'Completed' if done else 'Validation in progress'} — comparison checkpoint {s['updated_at']}.** The Drive pass has added **{s['new_verified_field_instances']} verified field instances**, including **{s['new_error_fields']} confirmed errors**, relative to the completed441-error baseline. Current integrated results contain **{s['current_confirmed_errors']} errors across {s['current_error_rows']} rows**.",'',f"Any field is verified for {c['any_field_checked']:,}/2,164 effects ({c['any_field_checked']/2164:.1%}); all seven for {c['fully_checked_effects']:,}/2,164. Repeated original statistics count as separate field instances; these are not representative error-rate estimates.",'','## Source coverage and exceptions','', 'The newly authorised Drive check recovered **129 exact complete primary sources** from136 previously unrecovered groups, bringing exact source coverage to **248/255 groups**. Copies comprise111 published articles,12 manuscripts/preprints/proofs, five theses/dissertations, and one primary unpublished report. These counts establish source identity/completeness, not verified statistics. All sources were independently hash-checked against the transferred mapping, with fresh PDF page/header/endmatter checks;72 automated content flags received separate primary-content review, including rendered scans.','', 'The seven exact-version exceptions remain separate: the complete1979 Srull/Wyer original has not been accepted as the requested2004 reprint; one matching Drive file is provider-blocked as abusive; Ritov/Zamir was not located; the Chan/Feldman Google Doc is inaccessible; and no primary replication manuscripts were located for three COS records. No filenames alone establish acceptance; no provider block was bypassed. See exceptions.json.','', 'Manuscripts retain their own pagination and version labels. The undated Ferrell primary report establishes data collection in2013, while its requested citation year2014 is not printed independently; main report PDF1–5 and primary author tables PDF6–9 are labelled separately. The related1979 article is held for edition review, with no silent substitution.','', 'The authoritative mapping SHA256 is29c160b7952005f0214ed1437d5dcd5dee48cb667bab701f177a161dd5f998cf. Primary artifacts and browser/Drive metadata remain private. The private archive check found zero differences across818 files (817 payload objects in the provider receipt plus the retained archive manifest), with two external mapping/receipt objects independently rehashed. Original handoff texts/PDFs remain unchanged. A labelled parent visual transcription of a missing diagram is retained as a canonical-text derivative, with separate source/render/derivative hashes.','', '## Blind validation and independent review','',f"The current-status filter leaves **495 previously paper-unavailable sides** from497 neutral sides; two already examined sides stay protected. There are140 source/side/chunk batches. **{finished} batches** have completed in **{len({r['taskId'] for r in tasks})} fresh native Codex jobs**, with at most three validators and the requested gpt-6.1-sol medium model/effort. Small source batches share bounded neutral jobs while retaining separate inputs/outputs. T3 MCP delegation is unavailable in this runtime; the native fallback and exact task IDs are recorded explicitly.",'',f"At this comparison checkpoint, {s['validation_side_attempts']} sides are integrated. {len(valid)} valid independent Argon replies cover {sum(len(r['items']) for r in valid)} field reviews; {len(reviews)} calls have been attempted. Nonobvious disagreements receive Gemini4 Argon(High) reviews with the original brief, coding context, source versions, previous findings, and unresolved objections. One stalled eight-field request was stopped by exact-owned prompt/process identity at12minutes and retried once as two smaller requests; no answer or error verdict is inferred from a timeout.",'', 'Extractors receive only neutral targets and named primary sources. Parent checks require full schema, exact source quotations, requested metric and same-test p-bound, uniquely identified study/outcome/sample/test, and explicit analytic counting units/exclusions. No metric conversion, numerical-coincidence target matching, row-order assignment, or significance-derived narrative success. Source-only acceptance never increments field verification. Unsupported quotes are quarantined until resolved; quote-only repairs preserve originals and do not change values, targets, metrics, bounds, or verdicts.','', 'Completed sides/author verdicts and every previously verified verdict/correction remain protected. All original/Linux/first-Mac/continuation completion records, deadlines, prior source metadata, and established scope holds remain unchanged. No historical schedule was restarted; no new schedule was created. Parent owns Git, exports, and PR155. No shipped workbook/pipeline/main-checkout/FLoRA edits, public PDFs, paid acquisition or incremental model spend.','', '## Confirmed incremental changes','', '| Row | Field | Shipped | Correction |','|---:|---|---|---|']
 for e in s['new_errors']:lines.append(f"| {e['audit_id']} | {e['field']} | {e['shipped'] or '(blank)'} | {e['correction']} |")
 lines+=['','Exact locations and reasons are in [field_changes.csv](field_changes.csv), with accounting in [summary.json](summary.json), task/status ledgers, original blind outputs, review prompts/replies, and protected integration records.','']
 (F/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
if __name__=='__main__':main()
